## fluent-korean (snflkd/fluent-korean)

The following material was adapted from the `fluent-korean` output styles in
[snflkd/fluent-korean](https://github.com/snflkd/fluent-korean), released under
the MIT License:

- `references/taxonomy-ko.md` — patterns `A-16` (개조식 불완전 종결) and `A-17`
  (필수 성분 생략 + 관형격 "~의" 과다), with their examples
- `references/quick-rules.md`, `references/playbook-ko.md` — the same two
  patterns, the protected-token expansion (code, identifiers, commands, paths,
  API fields, logs, error messages, commit messages), and the tense-injection
  guard
- `SKILL.md` and the `references/roles/*.md` role files — the same protected-token
  and tense-injection clauses

Modifications applied: the upstream "always complete the sentence" norm was
converted to this taxonomy's density-based `S2` severity with explicit exemptions
for headings, table cells, labels, and intentionally 개조식 documents; the
tense-injection guard and the "restore only what the source determines"
constraint were added so completing a sentence cannot fabricate tense, agents,
causes, or scope. Upstream global output-style guidance that is not AI-trace
removal was not adopted.

