## K-Humanizer (evergreentree97/K-Humanizer)

The following editing principles were adapted from the `k-humanizer` skill in
[evergreentree97/K-Humanizer](https://github.com/evergreentree97/K-Humanizer)
(commit `7e96372`, 2026-11-07), released under the MIT License:

- `SKILL.md`, `references/quick-rules.md`, `references/roles/monolith.md`,
  `references/roles/rewriter.md`, `references/roles/scanner.md` — the edit
  discipline rule (keep an edit only when it fixes a nameable problem; already
  natural text returns unchanged and still earns the top grade), from
  `SKILL.md` §5 "Stop when the text works" and `references/evaluation.md`
  "Edit Discipline"
- `references/quick-rules.md`, `references/taxonomy-ko.md`,
  `references/playbook-ko.md`, `references/patterns-ko.md` — the "no word is
  banned" keep-conditions on `~에 대해`, `~를 통해`, `~에 있어서`,
  `~와 관련하여`, `가지고 있다`, `~에 의해`, `진행`, `제공` and
  `~하도록 하겠습니다`, from `references/patterns.md` "Translationese and
  English-shaped grammar" and "Register and endings"
- `references/taxonomy-ko.md` (`E-4`), `references/quick-rules.md`,
  `references/playbook-ko.md`, `references/patterns-ko.md` — register
  consistency (unify unmotivated 합쇼체/해요체 mixing to the dominant level
  without changing that level), from `references/patterns.md` "Register and
  endings"
- `references/playbook-ko.md`, `references/roles/rewriter.md`,
  `references/roles/fidelity-auditor.md` — the paragraph-flow guard (keep
  connectors that carry cause, contrast or sequence; never add a causal link
  the source lacks; merged clauses keep each fact's own state, condition and
  time qualifier), from `references/patterns.md` "Sentence and paragraph flow"
- `SKILL.md`, `references/roles/fidelity-auditor.md` — the protected-facts
  extension (qualifiers such as `최대`/`약`, negation and exceptions, request
  versus offer versus promise in both directions, UI placeholders, variables
  and keys), from `SKILL.md` §4 and `references/evaluation.md` "Hard fails"

Modifications applied: the principles were fitted to this skill's S1/S2/S3
severity scheme, A–J taxonomy IDs, run-directory contract and A–D grades;
K-Humanizer's input modes (translation, English-source pair check), business
use cases, resume workflow and bare-Korean output format were not adopted.

